THIRD-PARTY ATTRIBUTION
=======================

The CPU core under `soc/rtl/core/` is derived from the third-party
open-source processor:

    openLA500 (齐物) — a LoongArch32-Reduced (LA32R) single-issue
    5-stage pipeline core.
    Original source: ../open-la500-master/  (kept pristine in this repo)

Local modifications made for this 2026 龙芯杯 (LoongArch Cup) SoC demo are
limited to:
  1. id_stage.v — the five TLB privileged instructions
     (invtlb / tlbsrch / tlbrd / tlbwr / tlbfill) are hardwired to 1'b0
     so the MMU privileged subset is not implemented (contest constraint:
     no TLB/MMU privileged instructions). `ertn` is preserved.
  2. All core files — a `timescale 1ns/1ps directive was added at the top
     for Vivado xsim timescale consistency. No logic was changed.

All other RTL under `soc/rtl/soc/`, `soc/rtl/periph/`, the testbenches
under `soc/sim/`, and the demo software under `soc/sw/` are original work
for this project.

This attribution satisfies the contest's academic-integrity requirement
(see Description.md) that all third-party code/IP be cited. The design
report MUST also cite openLA500.
